# Updated GUI media and Windows v0.2.3 release
Workstream-ID: lea-30
GitHub-Issue: https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/issues/30
Publication: PUBLIC_SAFE_PROJECTION
Source-record: Reviewed publication follow-through for completed dashboard and desktop work
Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: Publish illustrated current source and a verified side-by-side Windows release
Dependencies: lea-22, lea-23, lea-24, lea-25, lea-26, lea-27, lea-28, lea-29

## Purpose
Refresh the concise README and fictional GUI media to show the current action
and retained resume filename. Publish all completed dashboard and desktop
updates, qualify the matching Windows release and install it side by side.
Preserve private setup, earlier releases and independently running applications.

## Tasks
- [x] Establish explicit publication authority, an unused version and exact preservation boundaries.
- [x] Update existing fictional captures, screenshots and both walkthrough GIFs.
- [x] Review the actual media and align README, current guides and versioned release notes.
- [x] Review the complete public payload and run source release qualification.
- [ ] Commit and push only reviewed files with verified repository-local attribution and required trailers.
- [ ] Publish the matching version tag through the existing qualification-gated Windows pipeline.
- [ ] Verify exact hosted source, qualification runs, notes and release assets.
- [ ] Download and verify the actual assets and every extracted file before a new side-by-side installation.
- [ ] Exercise the installed frozen GUI and CLI offline without using private runtime data.
- [ ] Verify source-launcher, private-metadata and earlier-release preservation.
- [ ] Reconcile the issue, Project status and persistent backlink.

## Acceptance criteria
- [x] Current fictional media visibly show operation icons/names and retained or replaced resume filenames.
- [x] README remains concise, captioned and explicit about offline demonstrations and source-only dashboard extras.
- [ ] Package metadata, tag, hosted run and downloaded manifest identify the same exact release source.
- [ ] Published source includes all completed dashboard improvements; the Windows package includes the native desktop updates.
- [ ] All source release gates and actual installed-asset offline checks pass.
- [ ] No private configuration, applicant values, runtime data, continuity or unrelated work is published.
- [ ] Existing launcher/configuration and earlier installations remain intact; no independent application is restarted.
- [ ] Publication and offline qualification are not presented as live LinkedIn, clean-machine or human acceptance.
- [ ] One exact repository issue, one correctly staged Project item and a durable backlink represent this workstream.

## Completion evidence
At the start, cloud and checkout heads agreed. The prior stable releases were
v0.2.0, v0.2.1 and v0.2.2; the v0.2.3 tag and local version directory were absent.
The exact forty-six accumulated public payloads, twenty-nine prior tracking
records, selected private-file/native-preference metadata and six earlier
installed public entrypoints are baselined. Both effective Git identities are
the repository-local identity. The existing source launcher runs the checkout;
it does not fetch or select a release.
Thirteen PNGs and both looping GIFs are regenerated from fictional owned
widgets. Five focused capture cases pass. Actual media review catches and
corrects filename elision so the replacement resume is visibly different.
The final run GIF has nine frames over 17.8 seconds; the tutorial has seven
over 14.2 seconds. README links resolve, and existing counter anchors remain
stable. Updated guides and versioned release notes preserve source-extra and
offline-qualification boundaries.
An isolated public-source candidate passes Ruff, Black over 119 files, mypy
over 73 implementation files and all 868 tests. No private runtime inputs or
unrelated plugin are copied into that lane.
Publication and installed-asset checks remain separate pending gates.

